[?2004hroot@3ad32447bdd5:/home/user/releaser# cat > FIX_SUMMARY.md << 'EOF'
[?2004l[?2004h> # Release Tooling Fixes
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Issues Fixed
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 1. Version Bump Priority Bug (semver.py)
[?2004l[?2004h> **Problem**: The bump_version() function processed commit tags sequentially, returning on the first match. This meant tag order affected the version bump type, violating the priority rule (major > minor > patch).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> **Example**: ['SECURITY', 'FEATURE'] would return patch bump (2.3.2) instead of minor bump (2.4.0)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> **Fix**: Rewrote bump_version() to check ALL tags at each priority level before moving to the next:
[?2004l[?2004h> - First check if ANY tag triggers major bump
[?2004l[?2004h> - Then check if ANY tag triggers minor bump  
[?2004l[?2004h> - Finally check if ANY tag triggers patch bump
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> **Result**: Tag order no longer matters; highest priority always wins.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 2. Changelog Section Mismatch Bug (changelog.py)
[?2004l[?2004h> **Problem**: The utils.py config loader normalized all dictionary keys to lowercase ('security', 'features'), but generate_changelog_entry() used a hardcoded section_order list with mixed case ('Security', 'Features'). This caused section keys to never match, resulting in missing or misplaced changelog entries.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> **Example**: Security commits were missing from changelog or defaulted to 'Features'
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> **Fix**: 
[?2004l[?2004h> - Updated get_section_for_tag() to return lowercase section keys
[?2004l[?2004h> - Added section_display_names mapping for proper capitalization
[?2004l[?2004h> - Updated section_order to use lowercase keys matching the config
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> **Result**: Commits now appear under correct sections with proper formatting.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Verification
[?2004l[?2004h> Both fixes tested and verified:
[?2004l[?2004h> - SECURITY tag correctly bumps 2.3.1 -> 2.3.2 (patch)
[?2004l[?2004h> - Security commits appear under 'Security' section in CHANGELOG.md
[?2004l[?2004h> - Priority handling works correctly for mixed tags
[?2004l[?2004h> EOF
